Combined vk23 audit follow-up.

The generated mechanics projection for creature recharge abilities appears to parse ranges like "Recharge 5–6" and "Recharge 4–6" incorrectly by setting maximum equal to the lower bound.

Examples observed in the vk23 audit bundle:
- creature:adult-red-dragon — Fire Breath (Recharge 5–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 5, maximum: 5 }
- creature:ancient-red-dragon — Fire Breath (Recharge 5–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 5, maximum: 5 }
- creature:air-elemental — Whirlwind (Recharge 4–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 4, maximum: 4 }
- creature:blink-dog — Teleport (Recharge 4–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 4, maximum: 4 }
- creature:water-elemental — Whelm (Recharge 4–6) projected as { roll: "d6", minimum: 4, maximum: 4 }

This is not a source-coverage failure, but it is a deterministic gameplay bug: combat automation would under-trigger recharge abilities.

Acceptance criteria:
- Parse "Recharge N–6" as minimum N and maximum 6, preserving the correct d6 recharge threshold.
- Add regression coverage for at least Recharge 5–6 and Recharge 4–6 examples.
- Verify affected generated creature records regenerate with the correct recharge range.
- Ensure verify:dnd5e-srd-pack remains byte-clean after regeneration.

GATES-FIRST bead — implement EARLY, right after the thaw. Codify the known deficiencies as RED/failing gates that the modeling beads (.2-.10) then turn green. Layer on top of the still-green legacy gates (reproducible importer, source coverage 0, region ledger 0, suspicious records 0, hidden/control bytes 0). New gates in packages/core/src/rules/srdAudit.ts + tests, each expected to fail against the CURRENT thawed pack:
  (3) all class levels typed — no raw no-ref feature markers except typed subclass slots, no null numeric spellcasting placeholders (Ranger spellsKnown:null);
  (4) all level-up rows classifiable/applicable;
  (5) no missing feature headings (Rogue Thieves' Cant-style);
  (6) no mixed mechanical note tokens (Druid metal restriction);
  (7) feature/rule/spell/magic-item table links complete;
  (8) no duplicate table linearization in primary prose unless under sourceText;
  (9) choice coverage — every level-1/level-up player choice structured or explicitly out-of-scope with a named unsupported marker;
  (extra) no consumer overlay required for core character creation (ASIs, languages, spellcasting ability/prep, starting equipment present in pack).
Gates must fail loudly in CI. Writing them first makes the deficiencies machine-checkable so .2-.10 have an objective definition of done.

Add final review and finalization from character creation draft into the canonical playable character record.

Final review should show
- name/concept;
- level, class, ancestry, background;
- ability scores, modifiers, and method;
- HP and other derived values;
- completed required choices;
- missing required choices;
- warnings for stale or invalid selections.

Acceptance criteria
- Incomplete drafts cannot finalize and show actionable missing choices.
- Complete drafts finalize into the project's canonical character representation.
- Finalization preserves provenance/rules-pack IDs needed for later play/audit.
- Tests cover successful finalization and blocked finalization.

Identify and model the structured SRD data needed for complete level-1 D&D character creation. The generated rules pack is necessary but may not be sufficient if required choices are only stored as prose.

Candidate metadata
- class skill choice sets;
- starting equipment choices;
- spellcasting choice counts;
- class spell lists by level;
- ancestry ability bonuses and traits;
- background proficiencies and equipment;
- languages;
- tool proficiencies;
- armor/weapon proficiencies;
- features granted at level 1;
- formulas or metadata for derived values.

Design rule
The CLI should not parse prose to discover core mechanical choices. If a required character creation choice is only represented as prose, add importer/schema support or a deterministic derived metadata layer.

Acceptance criteria
- Inventory which required level-1 choices are already structured in the generated pack and which are prose-only/missing.
- Add or propose schema/importer changes for missing required choice metadata.
- Character creation engine can enumerate pending required choices for at least one martial class and one spellcasting class.
- Any remaining incompleteness is explicitly tracked in child beads rather than hidden in the CLI.

Add shared wizard-shell behavior for navigation and draft persistence.

Every step should support, where applicable:
- ? for help;
- list;
- search <term>;
- back;
- review;
- set <field>;
- save;
- quit.

Drafts should be saveable and resumable, likely under .eshyra/drafts/characters/<draft-id>.json or the project-standard local state directory.

Acceptance criteria
- review shows current draft, completed fields, missing required choices, and derived values available so far.
- save writes a resumable draft.
- quit offers to save when unsaved changes exist.
- resume restores the draft without losing state.
- back and set <field> allow corrections without restarting.
- Tests cover save/resume and at least one correction flow.

Add deterministic derived value computation for level-1 D&D 5e SRD character creation.

Minimum derived values
- ability modifiers;
- proficiency bonus;
- level-1 hit point maximum from class hit die plus Constitution modifier;
- spell save DC and spell attack modifier where applicable;
- passive Perception once skills are modeled;
- armor class once equipment is modeled;
- attack bonuses where practical.

HP must not be a required manual input in the default path. Manual HP override can be deferred as an advanced feature.

Acceptance criteria
- Fighter d10 with CON +2 computes level-1 HP 12.
- HP is not computed and no nonsense error is emitted when class or Constitution is missing/invalid.
- Derived values update when class, ancestry, ability scores, or equipment change.
- Tests cover HP prerequisites and recomputation.

Add docs/design/character-creation-cli.md capturing the agreed character creation UX and architecture.

The document must preserve the full design rather than summarize it away. It should cover:
- one shared CLI shell with rule-pack-specific character creation recipes;
- D&D 5e SRD as the first recipe;
- future Pathfinder compatibility without speculative Pathfinder implementation;
- canonical mode labels: Concept-first — I know what I want to play, and Ability-first — let the dice inspire me;
- why both modes matter: modern concept-first play plus 80s-era RPG nostalgia/discovery play;
- concept-first and ability-first step orders;
- shared commands: ?, list, search <term>, back, review, set <field>, save, quit;
- forgiving display-name/common-alias input;
- stateful draft preservation and save/resume behavior;
- dependency-aware validation with actionable diagnostics and no cascades;
- automatic derived values, especially level-1 HP;
- runtime generated rules-pack resolver replacing SRD_CATALOG;
- likely need for structured choice metadata beyond prose records;
- proposed components: RulesPackCharacterResolver, CharacterCreationRecipe, CharacterCreationDraft, CharacterCreationEngine, CharacterCreationCli;
- implementation slices, acceptance criteria, non-goals, and ADR candidate decisions.

Acceptance criteria
- Design doc exists in the repo.
- Open beads eshyra-4jiu and eshyra-x50w are referenced as inputs/overlaps.
- The doc is explicit that this PR is design/planning only and does not implement runtime behavior.

design:
Semantic-system design/evaluation only. Test the compositional reconstruction hypothesis before proposing storage:

- generic Eshyra DM charter;
- optional bounded campaign/table-specific DM charter;
- authoritative campaign/module/rules/state and campaign rulings;
- bounded generated campaign/character memory;
- optional latest bounded outgoing handoff;
- fresh provider-neutral model invocation occupying the persistent institutional DM role.

Use a four-arm ablation: A current baseline; B baseline + standing campaign/table charter; C baseline + outgoing handoff; D baseline + both. Define independent, falsifiable measures for behavioral/table continuity, narrative salience, non-restatement, authority compliance, stale-evidence handling, context cost, and provider/model-change robustness. Include normal close/resume and hard fresh-context cases. Reuse existing context, evaluation, trace, and audit seams where practical; ADR 0017 section 8 forbids a parallel proof system with no distinct failure class.

A seat is a conceptual composition unless evidence demonstrates a concrete producer/consumer/lifecycle that cannot be represented by existing or narrowly extended prompt, preference, memory, and provenance primitives. The investigation may conclude that campaign-specific style continuity has product value; it may not turn style, preference, or handoff intent into canon or rules authority. Evaluate the auditor independently and preserve its constrained mechanics/state jurisdiction.

